# Workflow

## Route

- Unclear need, prioritization or human/external planning -> optional Planner.
- Clear feature or bug -> Architect directly.
- Approved Linear issue -> Builder.
- Implemented issue -> fresh Reviewer.

Planner produces a self-contained approved brief for manual copy into a new Architect conversation. Never switch Planner and Architect Skills in one chat or assume shared-chat context.

## Authority

- User: intent, priority, approvals and human decisions.
- Planner: discussion, prioritization, read-only existing issues and external-action guidance; never repository access or Linear writes.
- Architect: repository-grounded architecture and executable Linear issues.
- Builder: one approved issue, implementation and self-test.
- Reviewer: fresh independent PASS / FAIL / BLOCKED decision from issue, diff and evidence.

Repository/Git defines implementation truth. Linear defines executable scope and Acceptance Criteria. Architecture docs/ADRs define stable constraints.

## Shared Rules

- Never guess between projects or repeat scope questions already answered.
- Search before creating architecture; prefer reuse, then extension, then creation.
- Use only relevant context. Architect may use a focused Repo Explorer; Planner may not.
- Keep role responsibilities separate.
- Builder proceeds only after a recorded `FRESH` or `SAFE_DRIFT` pre-build check; Reviewer verifies freshness and Change Surface.
- Pause for project ambiguity, product decisions, brief approval, development approval, credentials, permissions, destructive actions or major architecture conflicts.

Development is complete only when all Linear Acceptance Criteria pass, required verification succeeds, a fresh Reviewer returns PASS, and no blocker remains.
